/*  The shapes of C this compiler writes most: a name worked out from the program, a call, a pair of
    brackets. Each is source with holes (DESIGN *An axiom's text as a value*): the compiler's C is
    source all the way down, and only becomes text when a line of it is written out.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    // ── C as source, not text (DESIGN *An axiom's text as a value*) ──────

    /// The braces of a function being put together — where finished C is text already.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-open:
        Return [{].
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom to c-close:
        Return [}].
    Done.

    /// A function's text: its head, and its body as it was written out.
    Bind text to c-function-text, given (the text signature, the text body):
        Return "{signature} {cast c-open}\n{body}{cast c-close}\n\n".
    Done.

    Define c-language if-open, given (the c-language axiom condition), as [if (the condition) {] permanently.
    Define c-language else-if-open, given (the c-language axiom condition), as [} else if (the condition) {] permanently.

    /// Any one of these tests: `||` between them.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-any-of, given (the c-language axiom tests, the c-language axiom test):
        Define c-language or-also, given (the c-language axiom tests, the c-language axiom test), as [the tests || the test].
        If cast is-no-c on (tests), return test.
        Return or-also on (tests, test).
    Done.

    /// C written where a value goes — `Define x as […]` alone would DECLARE an axiom, not hold one.
    Define c-language c-verbatim, given (the c-language axiom code), as [the code] permanently.

    /// A C name worked out from the program — checked as one when it is filled.
    Define c-language c-word, given (the term name), as [the name] permanently.

    /// A pointer to a type named that way.
    Define c-language pointer-to, given (the term name), as [the name*] permanently.

    /// A text as a C string literal, quoted and escaped.
    Define c-language text-literal, given (the text words), as [the words] permanently.

    // The shapes that recur: a call of a named function, brackets, and `not`.
    Define c-language call-of-one, given (the term name, the c-language axiom first), as [the name(the first)] permanently.
    Define c-language call-of-two, given (the term name, the c-language axiom first, the c-language axiom second),
        as [the name(the first, the second)] permanently.
    Define c-language call-of-three, given (the term name, the c-language axiom first, the c-language axiom second, the c-language axiom third),
        as [the name(the first, the second, the third)] permanently.
    Define c-language call-at-line, given (the term name, the c-language axiom first, the c-language axiom second, the number at-line),
        as [the name(the first, the second, the at-line)] permanently.
    Define c-language bracketed, given (the c-language axiom inner), as [(the inner)] permanently.
    Define c-language negated, given (the c-language axiom inner), as [(!the inner)] permanently.
    Define c-language listed-on, given (the c-language axiom listing, the c-language axiom next), as [the listing, the next] permanently.
    Define c-language field-read, given (the c-language axiom holder, the term field), as [(the holder).the field] permanently.
Done.
